From c27c76215208d3c9de1a8456b830790abbbec4be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:05:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] libgcc: microblaze: use the generic C for 32-bit division

Replace the hand-written __divsi3, __modsi3, __udivsi3 and __umodsi3
with libgcc's divmod.c, udivmod.c and udivmodsi4.c, as iq2000 and
pdp11 do.  The assembly has no variants for the barrel shifter or the
other options, while the C is compiled for each multilib.  gcc calls
these routines through ordinary library calls, and with -mno-xl-soft-div
it emits idiv instead, so the change only affects cores without a
divider.

The C gives the same results as the assembly: 0 mismatches on about
700,000 boundary and random operand pairs per endian, in five
configurations.  Division by zero still returns 0, except that 0 / 0 is
now 1.

Instructions executed per call, mean, and estimated cycles per call on
the five-stage pipeline, mean (max), without options.  The cycles come
from a QEMU plugin that costs each instruction with UG984's latencies,
with no branch target cache; with a perfect one they equal the
instruction counts.  They are not measured on hardware.

		random		short quotient	long quotient
		insns cycles	insns cycles	insns cycles
  __divsi3  asm	 280  392 (401)	 224  316 (401)	 301  400 (401)
	    C	 210  265 (620)	  70   87 (107)	 450  568 (620)
  __udivsi3 asm	 256  358 (415)	 214  304 (415)	 305  409 (415)
	    C	 225  283 (615)	  66   82 (99)	 448  566 (615)

The C is faster on average for random operands and much faster when the
quotient is short, but slower when it is long, and its worst case is
about 50% higher: udivmodsi4.c shifts the divisor up one bit at a time
and then subtracts one bit at a time, two loops as long as the
quotient, where the assembly normalizes the dividend and runs one.

Keep mulsi3.S: the best C shift-and-add loop tried, which like the
assembly loops over the operand of smaller magnitude, was about 20%
slower on average and in the worst case.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

libgcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/microblaze/divsi3.S: Remove.
	* config/microblaze/modsi3.S: Remove.
	* config/microblaze/udivsi3.S: Remove.
	* config/microblaze/umodsi3.S: Remove.
	* config/microblaze/t-microblaze (LIB2ADD): Replace them with
	divmod.c, udivmod.c and udivmodsi4.c.
